        <section style="margin-bottom: 3rem;">
          <h2>Motivation</h2>
          <p>Python's built-in <code>http.server</code> is single-threaded — it blocks on every request. For file transfers, this means one download/upload freezes the entire server. NeoShare solves this with <code>ThreadingHTTPServer</code> while adding security features missing from the stdlib.</p>
        </section>

        <section style="margin-bottom: 3rem;">
          <h2>Architecture</h2>
          <pre style="margin: 1.5rem 0; font-size: 0.85rem;"><code>NeoShare/
├── server.py       # ThreadedHTTPServer + custom RequestHandler
├── index.html      # Responsive UI (auto dark/light)
├── script.js       # Fetch API: upload, download, navigate, stream
├── styles.css      # Cyberpunk theme, CSS variables
└── README.md</code></pre>

          <h3>Threading Model</h3>
          <pre style="margin: 1.5rem 0; font-size: 0.85rem;"><code>from http.server import ThreadingHTTPServer, BaseHTTPRequestHandler

class NeoShareHandler(BaseHTTPRequestHandler):
    # Custom implementations for GET, POST, HEAD
    # ThreadingHTTPServer spawns one thread per connection

server = ThreadingHTTPServer(("", 8000), NeoShareHandler)
server.serve_forever()</code></pre>

          <p>Each connection gets its own thread — file transfers don't block other clients.</p>
